address="Cham",
pages="367--396",
abstract="At CANS'20, El Housni and Guillevic introduced a new 2-chain of pairing-friendly elliptic curves for recursive zero-knowledge Succinct Non-interactive ARguments of Knowledge (zk-SNARKs) made of the former BLS12-377 curve (a Barreto--Lynn--Scott curve over a 377-bit prime field) and the new BW6-761 curve (a Brezing--Weng curve of embedding degree 6 over a 761-bit prime field). First we generalise the curve construction, the pairing formulas ({\$}{\$}e :{\backslash}mathbb G{\_}1 {\backslash}times {\backslash}mathbb G{\_}2 {\backslash}rightarrow {\backslash}mathbb G{\_}T{\$}{\$}e:G1{\texttimes}G2{\textrightarrow}GT) and the group operations to any BW6 curve defined on top of any BLS12 curve, forming a family of 2-chain pairing-friendly curves.",
